MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- GET /openapi/v1.json describes all 35 routes, so integrators can generate typed
  clients and CI can diff the surface for unreviewed breaking changes.
- /livez and /readyz split liveness from readiness. The existing /health probes
  upstreams, which makes it wrong for a liveness check: a model backend outage
  would restart every replica instead of degrading answers.
- The capabilities report gains a securityPosture block describing what is actually
  in effect — authentication, tenant isolation, plan-change credentials, SSRF
  validation, rate-limit partitioning — plus warnings naming each setting that
  leaves the deployment open. Matching warnings are logged at startup, so an open
  production deployment announces itself rather than being found during an incident.
- The parity matrix gains the rows this work shipped: streaming, default-deny
  authorization, per-account isolation, SSRF-safe retrieval, prompt-injection
  isolation, and the published contract.

Verified against a running Production-mode instance: startup warnings fire, the
contract serves, liveness and readiness answer, the stream delivers incrementally,
an anonymous plan upgrade is refused with 503, and both the metadata IP and a DNS
name resolving to loopback are blocked — the latter being the bypass the previous
hostname blocklist allowed.

Tests: 143 passing.
